  "id": "COMPOUND:30012 - PROTEIN:6095",
  "verbalization": "Pyranicin is shown to have a target of COLO-824 in all three visible paths, and COLO-824 is identified as a target of multiple compounds, including 1,7-Octadiene-3,6-diol, 2,6-dimethyl-, 20(S)-Ginsenoside Rg2, and Malvidin-3-(p-coumaroyl)-rutinoside-5-glucoside, all of which share a common target of Caspase-2. This suggests a potential mechanism by which Pyranicin may interact with Caspase-2, possibly through the modulation of a shared target in COLO-824. The consistent evidence across these paths implies that Pyranicin may act through a pathway that involves COLO-824 and Caspase-2, likely by influencing a biological process that is central to the function of these targets. The presence of multiple compounds with the same target in COLO-824 supports the idea that Pyranicin may exert its effects through a mechanism that is not yet fully understood, but is likely to involve the regulation of Caspase-2 in a cellular context. The integration of these findings highlights the importance of COLO-824 as a potential mediator in the relationship between Pyranicin and Caspase-2, though further experimental validation is needed to confirm the exact mechanism of action.",
